=3D"word-break: break-word;"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></span></p><p di=
r=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;"><strong>Do they kn=
ow what caused the crash? </strong>With the system that usually monitors tr=
ain speeds and movements not working, controllers at a centre in Madrid had=
 to manage traffic manually. A few moments after the system stopped working=
, the control centre authorised a train operated by Renfe to continue on it=
s journey, without a speed restriction. As this train began to accelerate i=
t approached a train operated by Iryo ahead of it on the same track, which =
had stopped due to the signalling failure.&nbsp;</span>
</p><p style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px"><span sty=
le=3D"word-break: break-word; color: #000000; font-size: 18px;"><span style=
=3D"word-break: break-word;"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></span></p><p di=
r=3D"ltr" style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;">At 8.53am, the Ren=
fe train struck the back of the stationary Iryo service. The accident has r=
aised questions about the chain of decisions at the control centre in Madri=
d. An investigation will also examine the age of the signalling technology.=
 The Madrid-Seville route is the only high-speed line in Spain still using =
the system and there have been four signalling failures on this stretch thi=
s year.&nbsp;</span></p><p=20
style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px"><span style=3D"w=
ord-break: break-word; color: #000000; font-size: 18px;"><span style=3D"wor=
d-break: break-word;"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span></span></p><p dir=3D"lt=
r" style=3D"margin:0;font-size:18px;mso-line-height-alt:27px">
<span style=3D"word-break: break-word; font-size: 18px;"><strong>What does =
this mean now? </strong>The crash is likely to have a significant impact on=
 Spain=E2=80=99s general election next month, our correspondent Isambard Wi=
